  "prompts": [
    {
      "turn": "native fourth planet",
      "text": "Add one independently orbiting dark planet to this system, named fourth. Use the installed checked public operations in one atomic transaction, including its host relationship and a true-scale observer-sky disk. Keep existing bodies, arithmetic and views intact. Fixed primary primary, detector earthward, radius 1.8 R_J, mass metadata 0.2 M_J. Circular orbit, semimajor axis 0.12 AU, inclination 90 deg, ascending node 0 deg, periapsis argument 90 deg, epoch 0 days and mean anomaly 0 deg. Mirror Ember’s GM/radius inputs and attached-orbit relationship, using fourth-orbit. Create sky-fourth projection, shape-fourth physical-radius geometry, disk-fourth mesh (reuse paint-ember) and place-fourth position binding with the same observer frame and metres-to-display scale as place-ember. The live occulting-body selection already includes new orbits. Preview if helpful, then commit inside the application and briefly describe the model assumptions."
    },
    {
      "turn": "native measurement",
      "text": "Add a reusable derived measurement and a visible independent plot through one atomic public transaction. Use the ID overlap-overcount for the generic arithmetic transit.flux minus naive-flux.value; specify a comparison meaning of overlap-overcount and reference earthward so the differing meanings are explicit. Bind it to a new plot overlap-bias-plot titled \"Overlap counted twice · fractional flux\" at x=1020, y=470, width=310, height=210. The quantity is the excess deficit in the naive sum; use the same normalized stellar-flux scale. Leave all existing nodes and links intact and commit this change."
    }
  ],
